{"contentRevisionId":189197284,"contentItemId":189197144,"assessmentRunContentId":189732507,"assessmentRunId":189732477,"title":"Sample - GTR - Summary (prod.)","supportedLanguages":["en_us"],"hasNestedSections":false,"hasBranchRules":false,"sections":[{"title":"OIR2AC0012B","id":184161323,"mode":"NYI","layout":"vertical-left","allowStimulusResizing":true,"stimulusSize":50,"sectionQuestionOrdering":"none","numberOfQuestionsToPull":0,"parentId":189197144,"additionalResources":[],"customFields":[{"name":"Testing Focus level 1","value":["Reading"]},{"name":"Section","value":[2]}],"nonAdaptiveOrderNumber":1,"nonAdaptiveOrderNumberWithScorableQuestions":1,"sections":[],"questions":[{"contentItemId":145439344,"contentRevisionId":174512730,"title":"  Stimulus title","objectType":"content_question_qti2_content_block","supportedLanguages":["en-US"],"defaultLanguage":"en-US","itemBody":"<itemBody inspera:defaultLanguage=\"en-US\" inspera:supportedLanguages=\"en-US\">\n        <div class=\"question-main-illustration\">\n    \n    \n</div>\n<h1 class=\"style-preset reading-text-title\" style=\"\">Political units in the history of West Africa</h1><h2 class=\"style-preset reading-text-subtitle\" style=\"\">Note: this is an extract from a General Training Reading text on the subject of political units in the history of West Africa</h2><p style=\"\">Ife, perched at the edge of Nigeria's forest, is thought to have come to prominence through its control of local products – including ivory, gold and pepper – in external trade. By AD 1300, its walled capital was at the peak of its wealth, with many shrines featuring elaborate pavements made of pieces of pottery, and a rich tradition of creating brass and terracotta sculptures, including ones of people richly adorned in ceremonial regalia. Many of these have survived. Subsistence for the large elite and artisan population appears to have been based upon small livestock and the cultivation of vegetables. Around AD 1500, the city of Ife declined, and the region's center of power shifted to Benin without any appreciable break in cultural tradition.</p>\n    </itemBody>","responseDeclarations":[],"templateDeclarations":[],"version":"2.1","hasRubricsMarking":false,"customFields":[{"name":"Testing Focus level 1","value":["Reading"]}],"additionalResources":[],"mediaInfo":[],"presets":{},"sectionNumber":1,"questionNumberingInSection":"0","countingNumberingItem":false,"fixed":true,"orderNumber":2,"category":"stimulus","parentId":184161323},{"contentItemId":145439342,"contentRevisionId":184161321,"title":"  Summary Completion (Productive)","objectType":"content_question_qti2_text_entry","supportedLanguages":["en_us"],"defaultLanguage":"en_us","itemBody":"<itemBody inspera:defaultLanguage=\"en_us\" inspera:supportedLanguages=\"en_us\">\n        <div class=\"question-main-illustration\">\n    \n    \n</div>\n<h3 class=\"style-preset task-table-heading\" style=\"\">Ife</h3><p style=\"\">The state of Ife adjoined the <textEntryInteraction expectedLength=\"15\" inspera:expandAutomatically=\"true\" inspera:type=\"dynamic\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE-1\"/>\n in Nigeria, and traded a variety of goods, including metals such as <textEntryInteraction expectedLength=\"15\" inspera:expandAutomatically=\"true\" inspera:type=\"dynamic\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE-2\"/>\n . Floors in religious buildings were made from bits of <textEntryInteraction expectedLength=\"15\" inspera:expandAutomatically=\"true\" inspera:type=\"dynamic\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE-3\"/>\n . There are many surviving examples of <textEntryInteraction expectedLength=\"15\" inspera:expandAutomatically=\"true\" inspera:type=\"dynamic\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE-5\"/>\n made of brass or terracotta. The population lived on animal products, and crops such as <textEntryInteraction expectedLength=\"15\" inspera:expandAutomatically=\"true\" inspera:type=\"dynamic\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE-6\"/>\n .</p>\n    </itemBody>","responseDeclaratio